# RADOLAN – Hourly Precipitation Time Series from DWD Radar Grids

R scripts to download hourly radar-based precipitation grids (RADOLAN RW) from the German Weather Service (DWD), unpack them into a uniform format and extract spatially averaged time series for an user-defined study area.

## About the dataset

RADOLAN (Radar-Online-Aneichung) combines precipitation measurements from the DWD weather radar network with hourly observations from rain gauge stations.

From the RADOLAN product series, these scripts use the **RW product**: hourly precipitation sums adjusted to station observations. Products with higher temporal resolution (5 and 10 min) exist, but are only quasi-calibrated and therefore of lower quality.

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Spatial coverage | Germany |
| Temporal coverage | 06/2005 – present |
| Temporal resolution | 1 hour (hourly sums); since 01/2023, a hourly sums are provided every 10 minutes |
| Time reference | End of the hourly accumulation interval (UTC); standard timestamp hh:50 |
| Spatial resolution | 1 km × 1 km (900 × 900 grid cells) |
| Projection | Polar stereographic (central meridian 10.0° E, standard parallel 60.0° N, spherical Earth with radius 6370.04 km); no EPSG code |
| Georeference | **None in the files** – projection and extent must be assigned after reading (see below) |
| Format | Binary RADOLAN composite format; `recent`: individually gzipped hourly files, `historical`: monthly archives (see below) |
| Updates | Continuously; data of past years are moved from `recent` to `historical` |
| Scaling | Raw values are hourly sums in 1/10 mm → converted to mm |

## Scripts

### 1. Download
The scripts download the RADOLAN national grids for a user-defined period.

| Script | Data | DWD source |
|---|---|---|
| `DownloadRADOLAN_HighFrequencyPrecipitation_Historical.R` | Historical data (monthly archives) | [hourly/radolan/historical/bin](https://opendata.dwd.de/climate_environment/CDC/grids_germany/hourly/radolan/historical/bin/) |
| `DownloadRADOLAN_HighFrequencyPrecipitation_Recent.R` | Recent data (individual hourly files) | [hourly/radolan/recent/bin](https://opendata.dwd.de/climate_environment/CDC/grids_germany/hourly/radolan/recent/bin/) |

### 2. Unpacking of historical archives

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `UnpackRADOLAN_HighFrequencyPrecipitation.R` | Converts the historical archives into individually gzipped hourly files (`.gz`), matching the format of the recent data |

The archive structure on the DWD server has changed several times:

| Period | Archive format on the server | Processing |
|---|---|---|
| 06/2009 – 06/2014 | `.tar.gz` monthly archives containing gzipped hourly files | Unpacked, files are kept as `.gz` |
| 07/2014 – 2022 | `.tar` monthly archives containing uncompressed hourly files | Unpacked, files are gzipped |
| 2023 | Nested archives (monthly archives containing daily `.tar.gz` archives) | Unpacked twice, files are gzipped |
| 2024 | Individually gzipped hourly files | No processing needed |

### 3. Time series extraction
Extracts an hourly time series of precipiation sums for a specified AOI and a specified start and end date.

| Script | Variable |
|---|---|
| `ExtractRADOLAN_HighFrequencyPrecipitation.R` | Precipitation |

**Input**
- Individually gzipped hourly RW files (`.gz`), organized in annual folders
- A `.kmz` or `.kml` file with exactly one study area polygon, e.g. created in Google Earth. An example AOI polygon file (Example_AOIFile.kmz) is provided for testing. The polygon covers part of the Hütelmoor peatland (NE Germany).

**Output**
Hourly precipitation sums (mm), spatially averaged over the study area polygon, one CSV file per year.

## Notes

The scripts have been tested for the historical data 2009–2026.

## Data source and license

Data: Deutscher Wetterdienst (DWD), Climate Data Center (CDC), [opendata.dwd.de](https://opendata.dwd.de/climate_environment/CDC/grids_germany/hourly/radolan/).
The data are provided under the [Creative Commons BY 4.0 license](https://www.dwd.de/copyright).

